{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/527454-questions-about-gifts","id":527454,"title":"Questions About Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T02:43:12-07:00","id":527454,"title":"Questions About Gifts","content":"Hi, I'm having trouble understanding exactly how players get Gifts. Sorry if this has been asked before, but I couldn't see anything specific on this when I searched.<br /> <br /> I am getting confused by what exactly the rules mean by facets and auspices, and how they work together. I think I understand character gen, its after that that I get confused.<br /> <br /> Say for example I have an Irraku Storm Lord, and I put the free Renown dot in Cunning. Therefore I have 2 Cunning and 1 Honor. As I have 2 dots in Cunning, I automatically get the first two Gifts of the Moon for Irraku. I get this bit.<br /> <br /> Now, I have the choice of two facets from the Spirit section. I assume I can only chose Cunning or Honor gifts, as those are the only Renown I have.<br /> <br /> So at the end of Character creation I have 4 Gifts, 2 from Moon, and 2 from Spirit. I'm hoping this is correct.<br /> <br /> If I want to buy new Gifts, this is the part that is massively confusing me. If I increase Cunning Renown, I automatically get the next Moon Gift. After that, the rules seems to become very opaque. I can pay XP to get a Gift, or unlock a facet, but I don't understand what they are saying.<br /> <br /> Help would be greatly appreciated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T03:49:56-07:00","id":527515,"title":"","content":"Ok, you've got your starting gifts more or less figured out, although just to be clear one of the shadow facets (&quot;Gift&quot; refers to the entire set of five) needs to be from the list of affinities for Irraka (Evasion or Stealth) and the other needs to be from the list of affinities for Storm Lords (Evasion, Dominance or Weather) Whichever two you pick (or one, if you got two facets from Evasion) are considered &quot;Unlocked&quot;, which is important later. <br /> <br /> If you were to purchase another dot of Cunning renown, you would get the third dot facet of the New Moon gift <i>and</i> the Cunning facet from one of your unlocked gifts or a Wolf facet, which are always considered unlocked automatically. If you've already got all such facets the free facet is saved until you unlock another Gift. If you purchased another renown you'd just get a free facet from that renown of an unlocked gift. Additionally you can buy additional facets from unlocked Shadow Gifts whenever you like for 2 experiences, and you can buy additional wolf facets for 1 experience. In both cases you need to have a dot in the corresponding renown. <br /> <br /> In order to unlock a new Gift you need to track down a spirit and have it teach you one of the facets that you have the renown for, which costs either 5 or 3 experiences depending on whether it was in-auspice or in-tribe or not. After that you can get new facets whenever you like, as with the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T04:22:27-07:00","id":527528,"title":"","content":"Thank you, that makes much more sense now. Hoping to run this soon, so I'm trying to get the rules down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:34:32-07:00","id":527604,"title":"","content":"Gift = Category of powers, think Discipline.<br /> Facet = Specific power, think a particular rank in a Discipline.<br /> <br /> Basically everyone makes the mistake of calling Facets Gifts, though.<br /> <br /> You have character creation down. Starting with 2 Cunning, 1 Honor as an Irraka would grant you the first two No Moon Facets, You would select two Gifts out of those favored for your Auspice and/or Tribe. Each of those Gifts would begin with one Facet that must be chosen from Cunning or Honor. This means you have 3 Gifts (No Moon, 2 different Spirit Gifts) and 4 Facets (first two No Moon Facets, one Facet from each Spirit Gift). If you had started with 1 Cunning, 1 Honor, and 1 in something else (lets say Purity) you would have 3 Gifts (No Moon, 2 Different Spirit Gifts), and 4 Facets (first No Moon Facet, one Facet from each Spirit Gift, any Wolf Gift Facet of your choice). In that case you could select the Cunning, Honor, or Purity Facets of your Gifts.<br /> <br /> After creation your options for Reknown and Gift-related improvement are as follows:<br /> <b>3XP:</b> Purchase +1 in your Auspice Reknown (Cunning, in this instance). If you do, you gain the next No Moon facet and one Cunning Facet for any Gift you currently have. If there are no Cunning Facets available, you hold on to the free Facet until you purchase a new Gift.<br /> <br /> <b>3XP:</b> Purchase +1 in another Reknown. If you do, you gain a matching Facet in any Gift you currently have (i.e. +1 Honor gives you an Honor Facet). If you already have all Facets of that type for the Gifts you have, then you hold on to this free Facet until you purchase a new Gift.<br /> <br /> <b>3XP:</b> Purchase a Gift favored by your Auspice or Tribe. Remember that Gifts are the categories, and purchasing a new one makes all Facets under that gift available for purchase. If you purchase a new Gift, then you immediately gain one of that Gift's Facets. You must have at least one dot in the Reknown matching the free Facet you select. I.e. to purchase the Wisdom Facet you must have at least 1 Wisdom Reknown.<br /> <br /> <b>5XP:</b> Purchase a Gift that <i>is not </i>favored by your Auspice or Tribe. Other than the increased cost, this otherwise functions as above.<br /> <br /> <b>2XP:</b> Purchase a Facet for a Gift you already have directly. You must have at least 1 dot in the matching Reknown (1 Purity Reknown to purchase the Purity Facet, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:12:44-07:00","id":527954,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you clearing that up, SoulGambit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T15:23:30-07:00","id":528132,"title":"","content":"As an addendum to Soul Gambit's great summary:<br /> <br /> <b>1XP:</b> Purchase a Facet of any Wolf Gift (all Wolf Gifts are always considered &quot;unlocked&quot;). You must have at least 1 dot in the matching Renown (1 Purity Renown to purchase the Purity Facet, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T15:55:39-07:00","id":528158,"title":"","content":"Oh, also whenever they get around to releasing more Moon Gifts those will be 5 XP to unlock and 2 XP for each facet after that.<br /> <br /> Actually would you need to hunt down a Lune for that or not? The book just says you can &quot;discover&quot; them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}